\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb8\f1\fs6\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb205\f1\fs24\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s8\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li720\sl240\slmult1\f1\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Taking\expnd-2\expndtw-12  \expnd0\expndtw0 Suspension\expnd-2\expndtw-12  \expnd0\expndtw-2 Measurements\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li719\ri374\sl244\slmult1\sb236\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 You make measurements and enter them into this screen much as you do for the Front Suspension.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Start by parking the car on a flat, level surface.\expnd13\expndtw63  \expnd0\expndtw0 First we must decide on what we will call the car\'92s centerline.\expnd13\expndtw63  \expnd0\expndtw0 Many people use a distance half way between the left and right tire patches.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The disadvantage of this method is if you change rim widths or wheel offsets your centerline can change.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This means all your measurements are now off also.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Therefore, we usually recommend the center of the drivetrain, which would be the center of the engine for most car\'92s front\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 suspensions.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This is a point which will usually will stay in one place.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The other advantage of this choice is the front suspension\'92s centerline is now the center of the engine.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This ensures consistency front and rear for most race cars, and provides an easy reference for most left and right measurements.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery365\footery647\margtsxn600\margbsxn840\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb1\sa1\f0\fs8\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li686\sl-20\f0\fs2
