pnd0\expndtw0 The car runs 16 second laps at the local low banked quarter mile track.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Ideally\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you could just\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 go to the Vehicle Library\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 and find an exact\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 match for this car.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 However there probably\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 is not\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 an \f6\b1\i1 exact\i1  \f0\b0\i0 match for any car already in the library, so we will have to build one by adjusting the specs for a car from the Vehicle Library.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb3\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li719\ri374\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 You can start with a completely blank screen for all vehicle specs by clicking on File, then New at the Main Screen. You can also blank out just the Engine, Front Suspension or Rear Suspension by clicking on File, then New at their respective screens.\expnd13\expndtw66  \expnd0\expndtw0 However, for\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 most\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 beginners\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 it\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 is\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 recommended\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 always\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 start\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 with a\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 example\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 vehicle.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 way,\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 for\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 specs\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 don\'92t\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 know,\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 there\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 is\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 already\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 a spec entered which may be close to matching your vehicle.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb2\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li719\ri437\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The LATEMODL.355 in the Vehicle Library would be a logical choice.\expnd13\expndtw66  \expnd0\expndtw0 (It actually doesn\'92t matter which vehicle you start with. Once\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you have\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 entered in the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 specs\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 for\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 your\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 car,\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you will\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 get\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 same\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 lap times\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 even if\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you start\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 with a\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Quarter\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Midget\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 or\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Busch\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 car. The advantage of starting with a car close to your car is that its specs are more likely to be accurate for specs you don\'92t know. Click on LATEMODL in the Vehicle Library, then click on Open to open it.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li719\qj\sl240\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Now\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 you\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 will\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 start\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 actually\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 enter\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 specs\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 for\expnd0\expndtw-